  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.06043v1</id>
    <title>Confucius4-R2T2: A Stable-Prefix Streaming ASR Model for Real Real-Time Transcription</title>
    <updated>2026-11-04T06:46:50Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.06043v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.06043v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Streaming speech recognition is increasingly consumed by machines, such as translators and voice agents, that act on each token as it appears. A token that is later revised costs wasted work or a wrong action. In this work, we present Confucius4-R2T2 (short for Real Real-Time Transcription), a stable-prefix streaming ASR model that never modifies its earlier output while maintaining high accuracy and low latency. R2T2 is obtained by post-training Qwen3-ASR-1.7B on 1,500 hours of Chinese and English audio while freezing its pre-trained audio encoder and projector. The adaptation is based on the concept of Longest Stable Prefix (LSP), a new notion that we introduce in this work. We prove that LSP is monotone under the prefix order, consistent with the full-audio output, and maximal among labels that equal a whole earlier output. Learning from LSP labels converts a full-context model into a stable-prefix streaming one without any architectural change. Extensive evaluations show that R2T2 brings streaming recognition close to the base model's full-context quality while delivering stable text with low emission lag. Its gains extend beyond the post-training languages, demonstrating a practical path from full-context ASR to stable streaming. We open-source the model weights and code at https://huggingface.co/netease-youdao/Confucius4-R2T2 and https://github.com/netease-youdao/Confucius4-R2T2.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.AI" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.SD" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-11-04T06:46:50Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>30 pages, 6 figures, 8 tables. Code and model weights available at https://github.com/netease-youdao/Confucius4-R2T2 and https://huggingface.co/netease-youdao/Confucius4-R2T2</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.CL"/>
    <author>
      <name>Daniel Huang</name>
    </author>
